        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "df90b426-6bc6-5037-8566-988d043dfc62",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Teide National Park, Garajonay National Park, Roque Cinchado, Tenerife, La Gomera, La Orotava, Canary Islands, Spain\n- People: Jordi Burillo Puig\n- Roles: retired professional tennis player\n- Concepts: World Heritage Site\n\nFacts:\n- Teide National Park is a national park located in Tenerife in the Canary Islands of Spain.\n- Garajonay National Park is located in the center and north of La Gomera, one of the Canary Islands of Spain.\n- Roque Cinchado lies within Teide National Park, a World Heritage Site, in the municipality of La Orotava near the Teide volcano.\n- Jordi Burillo Puig was born on 7 December 1972 and is a retired professional tennis player from Spain.",
